QA REPORT

Summary: The release adds Excalidraw+ promotional entry points and changes how editor sidebar controls and account links appear.

Key changes:
1. The editor gains comments and presentation promo tabs with “Sign up now” links, while the Library control becomes icon-only even in desktop full-panel mode.
2. A desktop Excalidraw+ banner appears in the collaboration controls and routes guests and signed-in users to different destinations; signed-in users no longer see the footer’s “Go to Excalidraw+” link.

QA checks:
1. Verify at desktop width with the full styles panel mode active that the Library control shows its icon without a text label.
2. Check the comments and presentation sidebar tabs and confirm they show “Make comments with Excalidraw+” and “Create presentations with Excalidraw+”, respectively, with a “Sign up now” link in each.
3. Confirm the “Excalidraw+” banner is shown in the desktop collaboration controls in both sessions, and that selecting it opens a new tab to the appropriate guest or signed-in destination.
4. Check the footer in a signed-in session and confirm “Go to Excalidraw+” is absent; check a guest session and confirm the encrypted icon remains visible.

Test areas:
- Main editor controls and sidebar (setup: Use a desktop viewport and an editor state with the full styles panel mode active.)
  * Verify at desktop width with the full styles panel mode active that the Library control shows its icon without a text label.
  * Check the comments and presentation sidebar tabs and confirm they show “Make comments with Excalidraw+” and “Create presentations with Excalidraw+”, respectively, with a “Sign up now” link in each.
- Excalidraw+ promotion in collaboration controls (setup: Have both a guest session and a signed-in session available, and enable collaboration in each.)
  * Confirm the “Excalidraw+” banner is shown in the desktop collaboration controls in both sessions, and that selecting it opens a new tab to the appropriate guest or signed-in destination.
- Editor footer (setup: Have a signed-in session and a guest session available.)
  * Check the footer in a signed-in session and confirm “Go to Excalidraw+” is absent; check a guest session and confirm the encrypted icon remains visible.

Uncertainty:
(none)

