QA REPORT

Summary: The release adds Excalidraw+ promotions in the editor and changes how the Library control is presented.

Key changes:
1. The editor gains a sidebar promoting comments and presentations with Excalidraw+, while a desktop promotion banner appears only when collaboration is available and enabled; signed-in and guest banner links use different destinations.
2. Signed-in users no longer see the Excalidraw+ link in the footer, while signed-out users retain the encrypted-status icon; the new promotion banner provides a separate Excalidraw+ entry point when its display conditions are met.
3. The Library control changes from a library icon with visible text on larger layouts to a sidebar icon without visible text, while retaining its Library title and toggle behavior.

QA checks:
1. Verify the desktop promotion banner appears when collaboration is available and enabled, and that its link opens a new tab for both signed-in and signed-out sessions.
2. Check that signed-in users do not see the former Excalidraw+ footer link, while signed-out users still see the encrypted-status icon.
3. Confirm the sidebar provides separate comments and presentation promotions, displays the corresponding content when each tab is selected, and uses artwork appropriate to light and dark themes.
4. Test each sidebar promotion link and confirm it opens a new tab.
5. Verify the Library control appears with a sidebar icon and no visible Library text, while its Library title remains available.

Test areas:
- Excalidraw+ promotions in the editor (setup: Use a desktop editor session with collaboration available and enabled, and have both a signed-in and a signed-out session available; also prepare light and dark themes.)
  * Verify the desktop promotion banner appears when collaboration is available and enabled, and that its link opens a new tab for both signed-in and signed-out sessions.
  * Check that signed-in users do not see the former Excalidraw+ footer link, while signed-out users still see the encrypted-status icon.
  * Confirm the sidebar provides separate comments and presentation promotions, displays the corresponding content when each tab is selected, and uses artwork appropriate to light and dark themes.
  * Test each sidebar promotion link and confirm it opens a new tab.
- Library access in the editor (setup: Open the editor at a layout where the Library control previously displayed its text.)
  * Verify the Library control appears with a sidebar icon and no visible Library text, while its Library title remains available.
  * Confirm activating the Library control still opens the Library sidebar.

Uncertainty:
(none)

