Summary: Text measurement, editing, resizing, and rendering have changed, so QA should focus on text layout and the appearance of text in drawings and exports.

Key changes:
1. A word that exactly matches the available text width now stays on one line; previously the equal-width case entered the word-breaking path.
2. Text height is now estimated as 1.2 times the parsed font size for each line, and text width no longer adds a 0.2-pixel adjustment; text creation, wrapping, and layout may therefore differ.
3. Bound-text font sizing during resizing is now based on available width rather than both width and height, and editing bound text now measures its dimensions even when it is one line.
4. Canvas text now uses a bottom text baseline, SVG positioning no longer uses the stored baseline, and the text editor is no longer clamped to its prior maximum width; Firefox and Safari also receive a 0.5-pixel editor-width increase.

QA checks:
